WEBVTT

00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:15,330
My husband is almost done with his eight rounds of chemo. I understand that this is a kill phase.

00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:21,970
What is used for kill phase after the chemo? So everything that we have

00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:31,650
him on is to help kill the cancer too. So this is the terminology that your oncologist gave you.

00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:39,010
Okay, the kill phase via standards of care would be the chemotherapy or the radiation that they're

00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:46,610
using. And then the, you know, the debulking phase would be a surgery. So this is your

00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:54,530
utilizing terminology from your oncologist. So after the chemo, you're doing all sorts of natural

00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:59,250
things to try to kill the cancer too and try to get your immune system to kill the cancer.

00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:04,050
You know, that's why he started with us. So that's what we're already doing. So

00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:09,170
if your question is, what is the kill phase for the standards of care approach?

00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:17,250
It would still be radiation. It would be more chemo. I am not, honestly, rarely here

00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:25,410
oncologists use this terminology anymore. So that's what they'd be using for something that they're

00:01:25,410 --> 00:01:27,410
giving to kill the cancer.

